+bool XmaContext::FlushTail(const XMA_CONTEXT_DATA* data) {
+  // The decoder output is realigned by kDecoderStartPadding, so the first part of the
+  // last decoded frame waits in carry_frame_ for a next decode that never comes when the
+  // stream ends. Real hardware has already written it; without it the guest mixer reads
+  // stale output (clicks, short repeats, beeps). Output it padded to a whole frame.
+  // If the stream continues later, only the padding (192 samples) differs from the
+  // decoder's real tail; sample positions stay aligned.
